# Core system and terminal packages. Everything here is required for a usable
# machine; anything optional belongs in an app of its own -- see
# docs/extending-with-apps.md.
base-devel
linux-headers
linux-firmware
mesa
vulkan-icd-loader
curl
git
rsync
openssh
# checkupdates, for handaan-pending and the bar's maintenance indicator. It is
# the only way to count pending updates without root: it syncs a private
# database rather than the real one, where `pacman -Sy` would leave the system
# half-upgraded. Without it that check reports unknown, not zero.
pacman-contrib
# arch-audit, for the same indicator's security tier. Arch ships no security
# repository, so nothing on the machine separates a security update from any
# other one -- the answer only exists in the Arch Security Team's tracker, and
# this is their own tool over it. Not optional despite the desktop running
# fine without it: the tier's whole meaning is that no card means no known fix
# waiting, and on a machine without this the check is blind forever while
# looking exactly like an up-to-date one.
arch-audit
mise
neovim
python-pynvim
ranger
ripgrep
fd
fzf
lazygit
make
xclip
wl-clipboard
htop
btop
pulsemixer
tldr
fastfetch
jq
pinentry
polkit-kde-agent
